    ],
    "license_hint": "MIT",
    "topics": [
      "memory",
      "evolution"
    ],
    "report": "projects/ai-agents-mem--turbovec.md",
    "screening_excerpt": "A 10 million document corpus takes 31 GB of RAM as float32. turbovec fits it in 4 GB - and searches it faster than FAISS. turbovec is a Rust vector index with Python bindings, built on Google Research's **TurboQuant** algorithm — a data-oblivious quantizer with near-optimal distortion and no separate training phase."
  },
