    "report": "projects/ai-skills--text-humanizer.blader.md",
    "screening_excerpt": "Humanizer makes AI-written text sound like a person wrote it, without changing what it says. It is built on Wikipedia's Signs of AI writing, the guide Wikipedia editors use to catch AI-generated text, and it works in Claude Code, Codex, and any other agent that supports skills. I'm thrilled to announce that shared drafts are finally here! 🚀 For months, our own team was drowning in files named final_v7.docx — and we knew there had to be a better way. Now two people can edit the same doc at once, with every change appearing live for both of them."
  },
